Fixes: https://github.com/nightwatchjs/nightwatch/issues/3086

[Major release](https://github.com/testing-library/user-event/releases/tag/v14.0.0) with a [major change](https://testing-library.com/docs/user-event/intro#writing-tests-with-userevent) in API:

```ts
// BEFORE
userEvent.click();

// AFTER
const user = userEvent.setup()
await user.click();
```

To make things easier, I've put `userEvent.setup()` in our `renderApp` function.

One thing to note is that `user.click()` now calls `setTimeout` internally between events (`hover`, `mousedown`, `pointerdown`, `click` etc.) which is [complex to deal with](https://github.com/testing-library/user-event/issues/833) in tests that user fake Jest timers. As a workaround until user-event provides [a better way](https://github.com/testing-library/user-event/issues/585) to deal with this, I've disabled this new `setTimeout` behaviour with `userEvent.setup({ delay: null })` as recommended.

Note also that a couple of our utilities like `selectExplorerNode` need access to the `user` object now, so instead of passing it as parameter, which would have been a bit tedious, I decided to return the utilities from `renderApp` so they have direct access to the `user` object in their closures.

```ts
// BEFORE
await renderApp();
await selectExplorerNode('...');

// AFTER
const { selectExplorerNode } = await renderApp();
await selectExplorerNode('...');
```

